  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A step-by-step wizard that loads an alignment, tip dates and a starting tree, checks how clock-like the data are, and turns the chosen substitution, clock, tree-prior, prior and variational-inference (ADVI) settings into a torchtree JSON config file to download. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
